    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Foreground system:&#13;
The data set describes the production of compressed air. Commonly either screw-type-compressors or piston compressors are used. For that data set a mix (50:50) of both technologies is used. The electricity consumption of the compression depends mainly on the respective pressure stage. The typical pressure stages 1.5 bar, 3.5 bar, 7 bar, 10 bar and 14 bar are modelled. The electricity consumption values are based on average industrial data verified with literature data.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability xml:lang="en">Compressed air for manufacturing operations e.g. industrial maintenance work, at production line as pneumatic tools, etc., and other final consumers.</technologicalApplicability>
